# `decode-ours.json` (37 MB) is committed on purpose: it is the profiler
# artifact behind the section 4.2 numbers, and it opens in chrome://tracing or
# Perfetto so the kernel timings can be re-derived independently.
#
# The matching vLLM-default trace is 73 MB and is NOT committed -- two traces
# would put 110 MB of binary in the history permanently. Its `.txt` table is
# committed instead and carries every number the README quotes; regenerate the
# trace with `bench_vllm.py --profile results/profile`.
results/profile/decode-vllm-default.json
